{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Loss Functions Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: MSE and Its Gradient"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mse(predictions, targets):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(predictions)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p, t in zip(predictions, targets):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total += (p - t) ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return total / n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mse_gradient(predictions, targets):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(predictions)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grads = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p, t in zip(predictions, targets):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        grads.append(2.0 * (p - t) / n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return grads"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Binary Cross-Entropy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The log(0) problem is real. If the model predicts exactly 0 for a positive example, log(0) = negative infinity. Clipping prevents this."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def binary_cross_entropy(predictions, targets, eps=1e-15):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(predictions)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p, t in zip(predictions, targets):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p_clipped = max(eps, min(1 - eps, p))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total += -(t * math.log(p_clipped) + (1 - t) * math.log(1 - p_clipped))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return total / n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def bce_gradient(predictions, targets, eps=1e-15):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grads = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p, t in zip(predictions, targets):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p_clipped = max(eps, min(1 - eps, p))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        grads.append(-(t / p_clipped) + (1 - t) / (1 - p_clipped))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return grads"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Categorical Cross-Entropy with Softmax"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Softmax converts raw logits to probabilities. Then we compute the cross-entropy against one-hot targets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def softmax(logits):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    max_val = max(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exps = [math.exp(x - max_val) for x in logits]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = sum(exps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [e / total for e in exps]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def categorical_cross_entropy(logits, target_index, eps=1e-15):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    probs = softmax(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    p = max(eps, probs[target_index])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return -math.log(p)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cce_gradient(logits, target_index):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    probs = softmax(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grads = list(probs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grads[target_index] -= 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return grads"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The gradient of softmax + cross-entropy simplifies beautifully: it's just (predicted probability - 1) for the true class, and (predicted probability) for all other classes. This elegant simplification is not a coincidence -- it's why softmax and cross-entropy are paired."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Label Smoothing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def label_smoothed_cce(logits, target_index, num_classes, alpha=0.1, eps=1e-15):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    probs = softmax(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(num_classes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if i == target_index:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            smooth_target = 1.0 - alpha + alpha / num_classes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            smooth_target = alpha / num_classes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p = max(eps, probs[i])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss += -smooth_target * math.log(p)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Contrastive Loss (Simplified InfoNCE)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cosine_similarity(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dot = sum(x * y for x, y in zip(a, b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    norm_a = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in a))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    norm_b = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if norm_a < 1e-10 or norm_b < 1e-10:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return dot / (norm_a * norm_b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def contrastive_loss(anchor, positive, negatives, temperature=0.07):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sim_pos = cosine_similarity(anchor, positive) / temperature"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sim_negs = [cosine_similarity(anchor, neg) / temperature for neg in negatives]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    max_sim = max(sim_pos, max(sim_negs)) if sim_negs else sim_pos"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exp_pos = math.exp(sim_pos - max_sim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exp_negs = [math.exp(s - max_sim) for s in sim_negs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_exp = exp_pos + sum(exp_negs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return -math.log(max(1e-15, exp_pos / total_exp))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: MSE vs Cross-Entropy on Classification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Train the same network from lesson 04 (circle dataset) with both loss functions. Watch cross-entropy converge faster."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sigmoid(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = max(-500, min(500, x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def make_circle_data(n=200, seed=42):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    random.seed(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    data = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = random.uniform(-2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y = random.uniform(-2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        label = 1.0 if x * x + y * y < 1.5 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        data.append(([x, y], label))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class LossComparisonNetwork:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, loss_type=\"bce\", hidden_size=8, lr=0.1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        random.seed(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.loss_type = loss_type"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.lr = lr"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.hidden_size = hidden_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.w1 = [[random.gauss(0, 0.5) for _ in range(2)] for _ in range(hidden_size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b1 = [0.0] * hidden_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.w2 = [random.gauss(0, 0.5) for _ in range(hidden_size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b2 = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.x = x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.z1 = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.h = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(self.hidden_size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            z = self.w1[i][0] * x[0] + self.w1[i][1] * x[1] + self.b1[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.z1.append(z)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.h.append(max(0.0, z))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.z2 = sum(self.w2[i] * self.h[i] for i in range(self.hidden_size)) + self.b2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.out = sigmoid(self.z2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self, target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if self.loss_type == \"mse\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            d_loss = 2.0 * (self.out - target)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            eps = 1e-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            p = max(eps, min(1 - eps, self.out))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            d_loss = -(target / p) + (1 - target) / (1 - p)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        d_sigmoid = self.out * (1 - self.out)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        d_out = d_loss * d_sigmoid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(self.hidden_size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            d_relu = 1.0 if self.z1[i] > 0 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            d_h = d_out * self.w2[i] * d_relu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.w2[i] -= self.lr * d_out * self.h[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for j in range(2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.w1[i][j] -= self.lr * d_h * self.x[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.b1[i] -= self.lr * d_h"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b2 -= self.lr * d_out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def compute_loss(self, pred, target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if self.loss_type == \"mse\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return (pred - target) ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            eps = 1e-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            p = max(eps, min(1 - eps, pred))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return -(target * math.log(p) + (1 - target) * math.log(1 - p))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def train(self, data, epochs=200):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        losses = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for epoch in range(epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total_loss = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            correct = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for x, y in data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                pred = self.forward(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.backward(y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                total_loss += self.compute_loss(pred, y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if (pred >= 0.5) == (y >= 0.5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    correct += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            avg_loss = total_loss / len(data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            accuracy = correct / len(data) * 100"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            losses.append((avg_loss, accuracy))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if epoch % 50 == 0 or epoch == epochs - 1:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                print(f\"    Epoch {epoch:3d}: loss={avg_loss:.4f}, accuracy={accuracy:.1f}%\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return losses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
